{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793742863,"nonce":"P4o9/6n+0AHsY+bej8LiOQbuPIY=","title":"Use a validated cached WASM preview for the landing demo","message":"User decision: landing Pocket Studio uses cached WASM; ordinary workspace previews keep host-rendered streaming. Add an explicit preview-mode/runner choice to Run Configurations and template/demo metadata, and make RunPart.previewAppBuild honor it before canPreviewAshui selects the surface script. Reuse AppPreviewBuild and existing target-aware RunPlan rather than introducing another compiler pipeline.\n\nBuild the immutable Pocket Studio release and its WASM preview ahead of publication. The initial app can run in the isolated preview frame before a remote session exists. Provide only a bounded browser-local demo file bridge until the session attaches, then preserve edits through the normal workspace binding. Do not offer arbitrary filesystem calls or production credentials in cached assets. Keep source/artifact provenance and app title metadata.\n\nAfter edits, validate exact input keys and compile only misses inside the visitor guest. Existing native .rayde/preview-cache validity must be tested at the canonical Linux workspace path rather than assumed portable from the Mac. Persist the last good picture with visible build/error state and replace it only with the matching successful generation. Closing/reopening or a tooltip must not destroy a valid frame. Done when a pristine demo Preview launches without either compiler, a source edit rebuilds correctly, unchanged retry reuses cache, and a normal non-demo Ashui workspace still takes its streamed preview path.\n\nPart of landing deployment: git-bug 56b531e22a0bf22913529f321d5b0f7d3ab02bef3d18192d73838675fff95704","files":null}]}